        {
            "block_label": "figure_title",
            "block_content": "NOTE 2 The online certificate status protocol (OCSP), defined in IETF RFC 6960 (as updated IETF RFC 8954) is a protocol used for obtaining the revocation status of an X.509 certificate. OCSP is an alternative to certificate revocation lists (CRL), OCSP is an online service. This means, that a backend infrastructure supports OCSP services in order to be able to use that service.",
            "block_bbox": [
